WEBVTT

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:04.600
The full SpliceGAIP analysis flow:
from a quantified splicing-event table to publication-ready figures and a report.

00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:10.000
Create a project: name it test, state the goal in one line ("group difference"),
and upload the results table quantified upstream.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:16.800
rMATS, SUPPA2, MAJIQ, LeafCutter and BGI RNAref are recognised automatically.
No FASTQ, no alignment here - the platform starts at the downstream end.

00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:23.000
"Smart analysis" runs an ingestion check first:
90 valid events, 20 samples, 100% FDR coverage, 100% delta-PSI coverage.

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:29.600
Sample groups, Tumor vs Normal, must be confirmed by a human before they are written.
The model never guesses groups - that rule is hard-coded.

00:00:29.600 --> 00:00:35.400
The pipeline starts. Six agents run in sequence:
data, QC, splice detection, statistics, annotation, interpretation.

00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:42.000
50%: the statistics agent is working. Chi-square tests with BH-corrected FDR,
plus a delta-PSI effect-size gate, to isolate events that genuinely changed.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:48.800
When default thresholds return nothing, it relaxes them adaptively by the observed
distribution and writes down why - rather than quietly moving numbers.

00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:55.600
Every agent reports status and results in real time:
the first four are green, annotation and interpretation are still queued.

00:00:55.600 --> 00:01:02.000
83%: the interpretation agent is drafting the biological reading,
drawing on gene annotation and literature retrieval.

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:17.500
All six agents finish and results land in the project directory:
standard figures, a ranked candidate table, an HTML + PDF report with full methods trails.

00:01:17.500 --> 00:01:25.000
Into "Visualisation": the volcano plot, delta PSI on x, minus log10(FDR) on y,
with the FDR = 0.05 threshold as a red dashed line.

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:32.000
90 events are in this run; the orange points pass both FDR < 0.05 and |delta PSI| > 0.1.

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:39.500
Switching to the PSI heatmap: top 25 events by delta PSI across 20 samples,
colour is PSI from 0 to 1, so a group-wide shift is visible at a glance.

00:01:39.500 --> 00:01:46.300
Figures come as 300 dpi PNG plus SVG, ready to drop into a manuscript.
No rerun is needed to fetch them - figures come from persisted project state.
